<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net472</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <!-- Sitrep.Propagation is BCL-only, ZERO external PackageReferences, same
       invariant as Sitrep.Core (KSP's Unity-2019 Mono + AppDomain
       first-assembly-name-wins collision risk). Do not add a
       PackageReference without updating that invariant deliberately and in
       the open.

       The "references no other Sitrep project" half of that invariant is
       GONE, deliberately and in the open as it asked. It used to say this was
       standalone because "a future Principia-backed provider would be a
       second IPropagationProvider implementation living beside this one",
       and that sentence contained the defect: an implementation cannot live
       beside this one if the interface it implements is private to it. The
       seam and its type closure now live in Sitrep.Contract, which is what
       an outside author can reference, so this project references Contract
       to keep implementing its own seam. The reference points at the
       boundary, never the other way. -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Sitrep.Contract\Sitrep.Contract.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
